-<div class="callout blue"><strong>概念</strong><br><strong>会计</strong>（accounting）是识别、计量、记录并传达经济信息的过程，让信息使用者据此做判断和经济决策，被称为「商业的语言」（the language of business）。<br><strong>服务业</strong>（service business）提供无形服务，收入是服务费，没有存货；<strong>商品流通业</strong>（merchandising business）买进卖出有形商品，收入是销售额，有存货和销货成本。<br><strong>记账</strong>（book-keeping）是逐日记录交易的例行工作；<strong>会计</strong>范围更广：汇总、分析、报告、解释财务数据，做调整分录和财务分析，遵守会计准则。<br><strong>信息使用者</strong>：所有者/股东/管理者、投资者、贷款人/银行、税务机关、竞争对手（讲义 p11），阅读材料还列了审计师。<br><strong>会计报告的 5 项要求</strong>：清晰（clarity）、准确（accuracy/reliability）、一致（consistency/comparability）、及时（timely）、合规（compliance）。</div>
+<div class="callout blue"><strong>English Explanation</strong><p lang="en">Accounting identifies, measures, records and communicates economic information so users can make informed decisions. Bookkeeping records day-to-day transactions; accounting also summarises, analyses, reports and interprets the records.</p><p lang="en">A service business earns fees by providing services. A merchandising business buys goods for resale: it records merchandise inventory and recognises the cost of goods sold when the goods are sold. Classify the activity before deciding which accounts and reports are relevant.</p><p lang="en">Start with the decision. Managers use internal information for planning; owners assess profitability, employees care about job security, investors assess whether to invest, lenders assess repayment capacity and tax authorities assess tax. Reports should be clear, accurate, consistent, timely and compliant so those decisions are based on comparable information.</p><strong>中文解释</strong><p lang="zh-CN">会计识别、计量、记录并传达经济信息，帮助使用者作出有依据的决策。记账负责记录日常交易；会计还负责汇总、分析、报告和解释这些记录。</p><p lang="zh-CN">服务企业通过提供服务赚取服务费。商品流通企业购进商品再出售：它记录用于转售的存货，在商品售出时确认销货成本。先判断经营活动的性质，再确定相关账户和报表。</p><p lang="zh-CN">先判断使用者要作出什么决策。管理者用内部信息规划经营，所有者关注盈利能力，员工关注工作稳定性，投资者评估是否投资，贷款人判断还款能力，税务机关核定税款。报表要清晰、准确、一致、及时且合规，才能为决策提供可比较的信息。</p></div>
 <p class="c-blue"><strong>例 1（Lecture U1 p5）</strong> Types of business: compare a Service Business with a Merchandising Business.</p>
