-<div class="callout blue"><strong>概念</strong><br><strong>会计循环</strong>是每个会计期间重复的一组标准阶段：①交易（transactions）→ ②原始凭证（source documents）→ ③日记账（journals）→ ④分类账（ledgers）→ ⑤试算平衡表（trial balance）→ ⑥报表（reports），然后下一个会计期间重新开始。<br>交易只有两种结算方式：现金（cash）和赊账（credit）。原始凭证举例：发票（invoice）、贷项通知单（credit note）、收据（receipt）。<br>三张报表：利润表（Profit and Loss Statement，又叫 Income Statement / Statement of Financial Performance）反映一个期间的收入和费用；资产负债表（Balance Sheet / Statement of Financial Position）反映某一时点的资产、负债和所有者权益；现金流量表（Cash Flow Statement）反映一个期间现金的流入流出。</div>
+<div class="callout blue"><strong>English Explanation</strong><p lang="en">The six-stage accounting cycle used in this course turns transactions into financial reports: transactions → source documents → journals → ledgers → trial balance → reports. It repeats each accounting period. Source documents provide evidence; journals record transactions in time order; ledgers group entries by account. The trial balance checks whether total debits equal total credits. Equal totals do not rule out omissions or postings to the wrong account.</p><p lang="en">For a cash or credit transaction, identify the evidence, journalise it and post it to the relevant accounts. Use the resulting balances to prepare reports. The profit and loss statement measures income and expenses for a period, the balance sheet shows assets, liabilities and equity at a date, and the cash flow statement shows cash flows over a period.</p><strong>中文解释</strong><p lang="zh-CN">本课用六阶段会计循环把交易转化为财务报表：交易 → 原始凭证 → 日记账 → 分类账 → 试算平衡表 → 报表。每个会计期间重复这一过程。原始凭证提供证据，日记账按时间记录交易，分类账按账户归集分录。试算平衡表检查借方合计与贷方合计是否相等；相等仍可能漏记交易或记错账户。</p><p lang="zh-CN">遇到现金或赊账交易时，先确认凭证，再记入日记账并过账到相关账户。根据账户余额编制报表：利润表反映一段期间的收入和费用，资产负债表反映某一时点的资产、负债和权益，现金流量表反映一段期间的现金流入与流出。</p></div>
