 <div class="callout red"><strong>易错</strong><br>① 把日记账和分类账顺序颠倒：日记账是第一手记录，分类账是第二手。<br>② 忘了标出循环在哪里重新开始：报表之后进入下一个会计期间。<br>③ 把资产负债表说成「一段期间」：它是某一时点；利润表和现金流量表才是一段期间。<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>Common mistakes: ① reversing the order of journals and ledgers: the journal is the first record and the ledger the second; ② forgetting to mark where the cycle starts again: after the reports it moves into the next accounting period; ③ describing the balance sheet as 'a period of time': it is a point in time; only the income statement and cash flow statement cover a period of time.</span></div>
-<div class="callout blue"><strong>常见疑惑</strong><br><strong>问：为什么叫「循环」？</strong> 企业的经营是持续的，每个会计期间都重复同样的 6 步。<br><strong>问：试算平衡表平了，说明什么？</strong> 说明借贷记录的金额相等，复式记账规则被遵守；但不能证明没有记错账户。<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>FAQ: Q: Why is it called a 'cycle'? A: Business operations are continuous, and the same 6 steps repeat every accounting period. Q: If the trial balance balances, what does that show? A: It shows the debit and credit amounts are equal and the double-entry rule has been followed; but it cannot prove no account was recorded incorrectly.</span></div>
