+<h4 class="kp-h">Accounting Conventions（会计惯例）</h4>
 <p class="kp-src">unit2 lecture slides accounting conventions.pdf · PDF p3–17；unit2 reading materials accounting conventions.pdf · PDF p1–4；unit2 tutorial guide accounting conventions.pdf · PDF p2–7<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>（资料来源）Unit 2 讲义课件 accounting conventions.pdf，第 3–17 页；Unit 2 阅读材料 accounting conventions.pdf，第 1–4 页；Unit 2 教程指引 accounting conventions.pdf，第 2–7 页</span></p>
-<div class="callout blue"><strong>概念</strong><br><strong>会计惯例</strong>是会计行业长期形成、所有会计人员默认遵守的做法：<br><strong>货币计量</strong>（monetary）：一切用经营所在国的货币表示（澳大利亚用澳元）。局限：通胀使不同年份难比较；管理水平等无法用货币计量。<br><strong>历史成本</strong>（historical cost）：资产按原始购买价、实际支付金额入账。<br><strong>会计主体</strong>（accounting entity）：企业与所有者个人的财务分开，一切从企业的角度记录。<br><strong>持续经营</strong>（going concern / continuity）：假设企业会无限期经营下去。<br><strong>会计期间</strong>（accounting period）：把企业的寿命分成相等的期间，通常 12 个月（如 2020 年 7 月 1 日至 2021 年 6 月 30 日）。<br><strong>复式记账</strong>（double entry / dual aspect）：每笔交易至少影响两个账户，保持会计等式平衡。<br><strong>权责发生</strong>（accrual）：收入在赚到时确认，费用在发生时确认，与收付现金的时间无关。<br><strong>一致性</strong>（consistency）：一旦采用某种会计方法，以后各期继续使用，便于比较。<br><strong>谨慎性</strong>（conservatism / prudence）：可能的损失尽早确认，收益在确定后才确认，避免高估资产和收入。</div>
+<div class="callout blue"><strong>English Explanation</strong><p lang="en">Conventions make records comparable and verifiable. The entity convention separates business transactions from the owner’s personal affairs. The monetary convention expresses measurable transactions in a common currency; it does not capture every non-financial factor. Historical cost uses the original transaction price supported by evidence. Going concern assumes continued operation unless circumstances indicate otherwise.</p><p lang="en">Use regular accounting periods to measure performance. Apply the double-entry rule so every transaction affects at least two accounts and debits equal credits. Recognise revenue when earned and expenses when incurred under accrual accounting. Apply methods consistently across periods and explain justified changes. Exercise prudence under uncertainty to avoid overstating assets or income without deliberately understating them.</p><strong>中文解释</strong><p lang="zh-CN">会计惯例使记录可以比较和核实。会计主体区分企业交易与所有者个人事务；货币计量用统一货币表达可计量交易，不能涵盖所有非财务因素。历史成本以有凭证支持的原始交易价格为基础；持续经营假定企业将继续经营，除非情况表明这一假定不再适用。</p><p lang="zh-CN">通过定期划分会计期间衡量经营成果。按复式记账规则，每笔交易至少影响两个账户，借贷金额相等。权责发生制在收入赚取、费用发生时确认。各期应一致使用会计方法，有合理变更则说明。面对不确定性应保持谨慎，避免高估资产或收入，也不能故意低估。</p></div>
 <p class="c-blue"><strong>例 11（Reading U2 Entity）</strong> John owns Lighting Warehouse. The business has cash $10,000, stock $16,000 and a bank loan $30,000. John's wedding ring worth $2,000 — is it an asset of the business?</p>
 <details><summary>看解答</summary>
 <p>按会计主体惯例，婚戒是 John 个人的财产，不算企业资产。企业资产只有现金和存货：10 000 + 16 000 = 26 000。银行贷款是负债，不是资产。<br>注：阅读材料写「The assets of the business total $56,000」，这是把 $30,000 贷款也加进了资产；贷款是负债，资产合计应为 $26,000。<br>Answer: Business assets = $26,000; the ring is excluded.</p>
