 </details>
 <div class="callout red"><strong>易错</strong><br>① 把「物有所值」当入账价：历史成本按实际支付的金额。<br>② 所有者自己拿钱不入账：违反会计主体，应记 Drawings。<br>③ 只记一个账户：违反复式记账。<br>④ 换折旧方法不说明：违反一致性。<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>Common mistakes: ① treating 'what it is worth' as the amount to record: historical cost uses the amount actually paid. ② the owner taking money without recording it: this violates the business entity convention and should be recorded as Drawings. ③ recording only one account: this violates double-entry bookkeeping. ④ changing the depreciation method without disclosure: this violates consistency.</span></div>
 <div class="callout blue"><strong>常见疑惑</strong><br><strong>问：谨慎性和权责发生制冲突吗？</strong> 不冲突。权责发生制决定「什么时候」确认；谨慎性要求对不确定的收益晚一点、对可能的损失早一点确认。<br><strong>问：历史成本有什么缺点？</strong> 资产的现值可能已经变化（例如通胀、市价上涨），账上仍是原价，但它可以用原始凭证验证，比较可靠。<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>FAQ: Q: Do prudence and accrual accounting conflict? A: No. Accrual accounting determines 'when' to recognise; prudence requires recognising uncertain gains later and possible losses earlier. Q: What is the drawback of historical cost? A: The current value of an asset may have changed (e.g. inflation, a rise in market price) while the books still show the original cost, but it can be verified with source documents and is relatively reliable.</span></div>
-<h4 class="kp-h">会计等式与现金制、权责发生制（Accounting Equation; Cash vs Accrual）</h4>
+<h4 class="kp-h">The Accounting Equation and Cash vs Accrual Accounting（会计等式与现金制、权责发生制）</h4>
 <p class="kp-src">unit2 reading materials accounting conventions.pdf · PDF p3–5；unit2 lecture slides accounting conventions.pdf · PDF p11–15；unit2 tutorial guide accounting conventions.pdf · PDF p3, p8<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>（资料来源）Unit 2 阅读材料 accounting conventions.pdf，第 3–5 页；Unit 2 讲义课件 accounting conventions.pdf，第 11–15 页；Unit 2 教程指引 accounting conventions.pdf，第 3 页、第 8 页</span></p>
-<div class="callout blue"><strong>概念</strong><br><strong>会计等式</strong>：资产 = 负债 + 所有者权益，A = L + OE，也可写成 A − L = OE（净资产）。每笔交易至少影响两项，等式始终成立。提款（drawings）减少所有者权益。<br><strong>现金制</strong>（cash accounting）：收到现金才记收入，付出现金才记费用，小企业多用。<br><strong>权责发生制</strong>（accrual accounting）：交易发生时就记录——赊销在卖出时就是收入（同时产生应收账款），赊购在买入时就记采购（同时产生应付账款）；把同一期间的收入和费用配比，得到更有意义的利润，大中型企业多用。</div>
+<div class="callout blue"><strong>English Explanation</strong><p lang="en">Assets are resources of the business, liabilities are obligations, and owner’s equity is the residual interest: A = L + OE, so OE = A − L. For each transaction, identify the affected accounts, decide the sign of each change and check both sides of the equation. An owner withdrawal reduces cash and equity; borrowing increases cash and liabilities. Buying a car for cash changes the mix of assets without changing total assets.</p><p lang="en">Under the cash basis, record revenue when cash is received and expenses when cash is paid. Under accrual accounting, record revenue when it is earned and expenses when incurred. For a credit sale, record revenue and a receivable on the sale date; on collection, increase cash and reduce the receivable without recording revenue again. Keeping these dates separate puts performance in the period in which it occurs.</p><strong>中文解释</strong><p lang="zh-CN">资产是企业的资源，负债是企业的义务，所有者权益是扣除负债后的剩余权益：A = L + OE，因此 OE = A − L。分析每笔交易时，先找出受影响的账户，判断增减，再检查等式两边。所有者提款减少现金和权益；借款增加现金和负债；用现金购车只改变资产构成，资产总额不变。</p><p lang="zh-CN">现金制在收到现金时确认收入、支付现金时确认费用。权责发生制在收入赚取、费用发生时确认。赊销在销售日确认收入和应收账款，收款日增加现金并减少应收账款，不重复确认收入。区分这两个日期，才能把经营成果归入实际发生的期间。</p></div>
 <div class="formula">Assets = Liabilities + Owner's Equity　　A − L = OE<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>资产 = 负债 + 所有者权益　　A − L = OE</span></div>
 <p class="c-blue"><strong>例 22（Reading U2 Ex 1-4）</strong> Lighting Warehouse: Ex 1 John introduces cash $30,000 as capital. Ex 2 the business buys a car with cash $20,000. Ex 3 the owner withdraws $2,000 cash for personal use. Ex 4 the business takes out a bank loan of $40,000. Show the effect on the accounting equation after each transaction.</p>
