 <p>按权责发生制，8 月 11 日卖出时收入已经赚到，应当记录：Accounts Receivable（Mel）增加 $50，Sales 增加 $50。<br>9 月 5 日 Mel 付款时不是新的销售：Cash at Bank 增加 $50，Accounts Receivable 减少 $50。<br>Joel 的做法把收入推迟到 9 月，8 月的销售被少记、9 月被多记，两个期间的利润都不准确，也漏记了 8 月底的应收账款。</p>
 </details>
 <div class="callout red"><strong>易错</strong><br>① 把提款当费用：提款减少所有者权益，不是费用。<br>② 用现金买资产时说「资产增加了」：一增一减，总资产不变。<br>③ 权责发生制下收款时再记一次收入：收入只在卖出时记一次。<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>Common mistakes: ① treating drawings as an expense: drawings reduce owner's equity and are not an expense; ② saying 'assets increased' when buying an asset with cash: one increases and one decreases, so total assets are unchanged; ③ under accrual accounting recording revenue again when cash is received: revenue is recorded only once, at the time of sale.</span></div>
-<div class="callout blue"><strong>常见疑惑</strong><br><strong>问：贷款增加了现金，为什么所有者权益不变？</strong> 借来的钱要还，对应负债增加：资产 +40 000 = 负债 +40 000。<br><strong>问：现金制和权责发生制，哪种利润更准？</strong> 权责发生制，因为它把同一期间赚到的收入和为此发生的费用配在一起。<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>FAQ: Q: A loan increased cash, so why does owner's equity not change? A: The borrowed money has to be repaid, so liabilities increase correspondingly: assets +40 000 = liabilities +40 000. Q: Which gives a more accurate profit, cash accounting or accrual accounting? A: Accrual accounting, because it matches the revenue earned in the same period with the expenses incurred to earn it.</span></div>
+<div class="callout blue"><strong>常见疑惑</strong><br><strong>问：贷款增加了现金，为什么所有者权益不变？</strong> 借来的钱要还，对应负债增加：资产 +40 000 = 负债 +40 000。<br><strong>问：为什么权责发生制更适合衡量期间利润？</strong> 权责发生制，因为它把同一期间赚到的收入和为此发生的费用配在一起。<br><span class='bi-add' style='display:block;color:#171717;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;margin-top:6px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid #b03030;background:#faf8f3;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.7;'>FAQ: Q: A loan increased cash, so why does owner's equity not change? A: The borrowed money has to be repaid, so liabilities increase correspondingly: assets +40 000 = liabilities +40 000. Q: Why is accrual accounting more useful for measuring profit for a period? A: Accrual accounting, because it matches the revenue earned in the same period with the expenses incurred to earn it.</span></div>
